// EXPECT: PASS
// Scope BOUNDARY for the 2026-07-21 middle-option: it extends static discharge to INTEGER asserts
// only. A FLOAT in-body `assert` in a NON-contract function stays FAIL-OPEN (runtime-enforced) — the
// documented stance for genuinely-unmodelable asserts is deliberately UNCHANGED (floats/strings are
// runtime checks outside a contract). So `x > 0.0` is not statically modeled and `check` passes even
// though it is only a runtime backstop. This locks the boundary: if a future change extends param
// modeling to floats, this fixture flips to FAIL and forces a conscious re-decision rather than a
// silent stance drift.
pub fn fp(x: f64) {
    assert(x > 0.0);
}

fn main() {
    fp(1.5);
}
